": "toolu_01UmhcQW5ote3aL7CUTcj1jT", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 382108, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UmhcQW5ote3aL7CUTcj1jT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 385774, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, the comment on `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** The CI run on that branch (run ci-0001) passed.\n\nThe advisory tool didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check what it says. I went by the comment in the code and the test.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Policy says it needs a code owner's approval first.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011RWDxa2ZQaCVL9U35JcSAE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W8caT6cUii3zHUBjVvSov3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YYfGujodgMqRKKNwPksRx4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CUBaZYW2VTYTDZ6KydoQsP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HxAhq1idkVEojGnksfmPiM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ATtWxY6Z11xtZdExaxNLpF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Smsf9gEE7hgSjJMAVmfQF4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UmhcQW5ote3aL7CUTcj1jT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`round_money` in `src/money.py` was documented as using banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, the comment on `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** The CI run on that branch (run ci-0001) passed.\n\nThe advisory tool didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check what it says. I went by the comment in the code and the test.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Policy says it needs a code owner's approval first.", "type": "text"}]}]}